p:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: What Owners Should Know</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Missouri</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession sale</li><li>Turn the Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Missouri House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Missouri law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>No action to recover lands or possession may be maintained unless plaintiff or predecessor was seized or possessed of the premises within ten years before the action (10-year limitation underlying adverse possession). (RSMo 516.010; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=516.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Eviction-type possession remedy via unlawful detainer/rent-and-possession procedure exists for landlords when rent is not paid as agreed. (RSMo 535.010; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Missouri?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Missouri houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Missouri house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Missouri attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-eviction-notice/'>Missouri Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-probate-laws/'>Missouri Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Missouri guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/'>We buy houses in Missouri</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=516.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 516.010</a></li><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 535.010</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Missouri house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Missouri attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Missouri\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Missouri squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "missouri squatters rights"}, {"slug": "missouri-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Missouri</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Missouri House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Missouri statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>A landlord may not demand or receive a security deposit in excess of two months&#x27; rent. (RSMo 535.300; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.300' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Within thirty days after termination of the tenancy the landlord must furnish a written itemized list of damages withheld, with the balance of the deposit. (RSMo 535.300; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.300' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If the landlord wrongfully withholds the deposit, the tenant recovers twice the amount wrongfully withheld. (RSMo 535.300; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.300' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A tenancy at will/sufferance or for less than one year, and unwritten month-to-month tenancies, terminate on one month&#x27;s written notice; month-to-month ends on a periodic rent-paying date not less than one month after receipt of notice. (RSMo 441.060; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=441.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Mobile-home lot tenancies under one year: landlord notice not sooner than sixty days from the date rent next becomes due. (RSMo 441.060(2); <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=441.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Missouri?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Missouri houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-eviction-notice/'>Missouri Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-probate-laws/'>Missouri Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Missouri guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/'>We buy houses in Missouri</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.300' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 535.300</a></li><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=441.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 441.060</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Missouri\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights", "rank_math_description": "Missouri landlord tenant law and tenant rights: deposits, notices, entry and selling a rented house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "missouri tenant rights"}, {"slug": "missouri-eviction-notice", "title": "Missouri Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Missouri Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Missouri</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Missouri Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Missouri Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Missouri Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Missouri House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Missouri law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>If rent is not paid as agreed, the landlord may dispossess the tenant and subtenants and recover possession in the manner provided in chapter 535. (RSMo 535.010; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Month-to-month/at-will termination: one month&#x27;s written notice. (RSMo 441.060; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=441.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Missouri?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Missouri houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-probate-laws/'>Missouri Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Missouri guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/'>We buy houses in Missouri</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=535.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 535.010</a></li><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=441.060' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 441.060</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Missouri Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Missouri\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Missouri Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Missouri Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Missouri eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "missouri eviction notice"}, {"slug": "missouri-probate-laws", "title": "Missouri Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Missouri Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Missouri</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Missouri Probate Laws: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Missouri Probate Laws sale</li><li>Turn the Missouri Probate Laws offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Missouri House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Missouri probate law decides who inherits when there is no will, when a small estate can skip full probate, and who can sign a deed for an inherited house.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Small estate (distribution without letters, including real property) if entire estate less liens, debts and encumbrances does not exceed $40,000 and 30 days have elapsed since death with no pending letters application. (RSMo 473.097(1)-(2); <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.097' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Small estate requires a bond (unless court dispenses) and fee; distributees establish right to real estate by recording the affidavit and clerk&#x27;s certificate with the recorder of deeds. (RSMo 473.097; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.097' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A will must be presented for probate within one year of death (when no notice of letters given), or 6 months after first publication of notice of letters; a will not timely presented is forever barred. (RSMo 473.050; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.050' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Letters of administration generally cannot issue unless applied for within one year from date of death. (RSMo 473.050; <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.050' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Surviving spouse receives the entire intestate estate if there is no surviving issue of the decedent. (RSMo 474.010(1)(a); <a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=474.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Missouri?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Missouri houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Missouri Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Missouri Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-eviction-notice/'>Missouri Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Missouri guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/'>We buy houses in Missouri</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.097' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 473.097(1)-(2)</a></li><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=473.050' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 473.050</a></li><li><a href='https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=474.010' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>RSMo 474.010(1)(a)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Missouri Probate Laws, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Missouri\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-missouri/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Missouri Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/missouri-probate-laws/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Missouri Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales", "rank_math_description": "Missouri probate laws: who inherits without a will, small estate rules, deadlines and selling an inherited house. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "missouri probate laws"}]